# `docker compose up --build` sends the repo root as the build context: only what the Dockerfile
# copies goes in (no .venv, .git, swarm projects with their databases and dreamteam.toml keys).
# `dreamteam sandbox` assembles its own clean context (docker.build_context).
*
!pyproject.toml
!README.md
!Dockerfile
!src/
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
**/.dreamteam
